const blogPosts = [
  ['best-ai-personal-stylist-app','Best AI personal stylist app','best AI personal stylist app','The best AI personal stylist app depends on the job you need done. Style BFF is built for people who want personal guidance, occasion outfits, a digital wardrobe and a visual try-on on their own photo—not just a generic outfit idea.','Compare the job, not the marketing','Start with the decision you repeat: choosing an outfit, organizing a closet, finding your colors or checking a saved look. A useful stylist should connect that decision to your real life, not only show inspiration images.','Style BFF starts with you','Style BFF combines a Style Profile, digital wardrobe, occasion-based outfit ideas and try-on from supported links. That is especially useful when you want to answer “does this suit me?” before you get dressed or buy.'],
  ['can-ai-show-me-what-an-outfit-looks-like-on-me','Can AI show me what an outfit looks like on me?','can AI show me what an outfit looks like on me','Yes. AI virtual try-on can create a styling preview of an outfit on your own photo. It is most useful for comparing overall color, silhouette and mood before you wear or shop a look.','Use try-on as a visual decision tool','Choose a clear photo, bring in a saved or shared look, and compare the result with the colors and proportions you usually like. A preview is a practical way to narrow choices before you spend time getting dressed.','What Style BFF adds','Style BFF pairs the preview with your personal Style Profile and outfit guidance. That makes the result more useful than a one-off generated image because the suggestion can reflect your preferences, occasion and wardrobe.'],
  ['how-to-try-on-pinterest-outfits-on-yourself','How to try on Pinterest outfits on yourself','try on Pinterest outfits on yourself','To try a Pinterest outfit on yourself, save or share a supported public Pinterest link to Style BFF, then use your own photo for a virtual styling preview.','Start with the look you saved','Choose an image that shows the outfit clearly. The better the visible clothing, layers and proportions, the more useful the styling preview will be. Save the result alongside the original inspiration so you can compare both.','Make the inspiration wearable','An inspiration image is a direction, not a uniform. Use your palette, body guidance and what you already own to keep the part you love—perhaps the color contrast, shape or layering—while making it feel like you.','Try the link in Style BFF','Style BFF is designed for supported Pinterest, Instagram and store links. It helps you see the direction on your own photo and then rebuild it from your own closet when possible.'],
  ['how-to-try-on-instagram-outfits-before-you-buy','How to try on Instagram outfits before you buy','try on Instagram outfits before buying','You can use a supported public Instagram look as a starting point for a virtual try-on. The goal is not an exact fit guarantee; it is to see whether the outfit direction feels right on you before you buy.','Choose a clear public post','Use a post where the outfit is visible and the link can be shared. Private, deleted or restricted posts may not be available to import.','Check the part that matters most','Look at the near-face color, the overall proportion and the way the outfit fits the occasion. Those are usually more useful than treating a generated result as a precise size or fabric prediction.','Use Style BFF for the next step','Share a supported Instagram link with Style BFF to try the look on your own photo. Then save it, adjust the direction or use it as a reference for pieces already in your digital wardrobe.'],
  ['can-i-try-on-clothes-from-any-store-link-with-ai','Can I try on clothes from a store link with AI?','try on clothes from a store link with AI','Many public product links can become a starting point for AI virtual try-on. With Style BFF, share a supported store link to explore how the look may work on you before adding it to your cart.','Use a product page with clear images','A front-facing image, visible garment details and a public page give you the best starting point. Product availability and link support can change, so treat the preview as styling help rather than retailer inventory data.','Separate style from fit','Virtual try-on is helpful for color, silhouette and outfit direction. Check the retailer’s measurements, fabric notes, reviews and return policy for sizing and construction.','Why try it in Style BFF','Style BFF connects a supported store-link preview to your style profile and wardrobe. This helps you ask a more useful question than “is this trendy?”: “will this earn a place in my closet?”'],
  ['ai-stylist-vs-ai-outfit-generator','AI stylist vs AI outfit generator','AI stylist vs AI outfit generator','An AI outfit generator creates ideas on demand. An AI personal stylist is more useful when it learns your preferences, considers your occasion and works with the clothes you own over time.','What an outfit generator does','Generators are good for visual inspiration, themes and quick combinations. They often do not remember your wardrobe, color preferences or what you need to wear on a real Tuesday.','What a personal stylist adds','A stylist can turn your inputs into repeatable decisions: which colors to favor, what to wear for a specific plan and how to create more outfits from your actual closet.','Why Style BFF is different','Style BFF combines personal guidance, a digital wardrobe, occasion outfits and visual try-on. It is designed to make getting dressed easier, not simply create another image to scroll past.'],
  ['what-should-i-wear-today-from-my-closet','What should I wear today from my closet?','what should I wear today','Start with your plan, the weather and the clothes you can actually wear. Then choose one reliable base, one near-face color and shoes that match the level of formality you need.','Use a three-question filter',['Where are you going and how formal is it?','What does the weather require?','Which items make you feel comfortable and like yourself?'],'Build one outfit before five options','Pick the strongest answer first. For example: dark trousers, a color that flatters you near your face, and an outer layer that matches the setting. You can add personality with one accessory instead of restarting the whole outfit.','Let Style BFF narrow the choice','Style BFF creates occasion-based outfit ideas from your profile and digital wardrobe. It is useful when you want a quick, personal starting point rather than a generic style list.'],
  ['nothing-to-wear-use-what-you-own','I have nothing to wear: use what you own','nothing to wear but a full closet','A full closet can still feel unusable when your clothes are hard to see, hard to combine or no longer match your life. The fastest fix is to identify your dependable pieces and build a few repeatable outfit formulas around them.','Find your dependable base','Pull out the pieces you reach for when you have five minutes: the trousers that fit, the top color that feels good and the shoe you can walk in. These are the building blocks, not boring fallback choices.','Create useful combinations',['Pair one reliable bottom with three different near-face tops.','Use one jacket or layer to make casual pieces work for work or dinner.','Save the outfits that work so you do not have to rediscover them every morning.'],'How Style BFF helps','Add the clothes you want to wear more to your digital wardrobe. Style BFF can suggest new combinations and occasion outfits from the pieces you already own.'],
  ['how-to-build-a-digital-closet','How to build a digital closet','how to build a digital closet','A digital closet is a visual record of the clothes you own. Start small: add the pieces you wear most, group them by type, then use the collection to build outfits for real plans.','Do not start with every item','Begin with your core rotation: favorite tops, bottoms, layers, shoes and bags. A closet that helps you get dressed is more valuable than a perfect inventory you never finish.','Make each item useful','Use clear images, simple labels and a realistic view of what is clean, fits and suits your current life. Add seasonal or occasion notes when they help you decide faster.','Use Style BFF as your wardrobe layer','Style BFF turns your digital wardrobe into outfit combinations and occasion recommendations. It can also help you see which pieces work together before you start shopping for more.'],
  ['how-to-find-wardrobe-gaps-before-shopping','How to find wardrobe gaps before shopping','how to find wardrobe gaps','A wardrobe gap is not simply something you do not own. It is a missing piece that would make several existing clothes easier to wear for the occasions you actually have.','Look for repeated dead ends','Notice where outfits stop working: perhaps your tops do not work with your work trousers, your shoes do not match your dresses, or you lack a layer for a temperature change.','Choose connector pieces','The most useful additions usually work across multiple outfits. Before buying, list at least three combinations the item would complete using clothes you already own.','Use Complete the Closet in Style BFF','Style BFF can help identify the two or three pieces that could unlock more combinations in your digital wardrobe, so the next purchase has a clear job.'],
  ['is-ai-virtual-try-on-accurate','Is AI virtual try-on accurate?','is AI virtual try-on accurate','AI virtual try-on can be accurate enough to compare color, silhouette and overall styling direction. It is not a guarantee of size, fit, fabric movement, texture or exact garment construction.','What it is good at','Use a preview to decide whether you like a look near your face, whether the outfit feels right for an occasion and whether the overall proportion fits your style direction.','What it cannot replace','Always use the seller’s size chart, product measurements, material details and return policy. A virtual image cannot tell you how a garment will feel or fit in motion.','How Style BFF uses it','Style BFF treats virtual try-on as part of styling: a useful visual answer after you consider your profile, occasion and wardrobe. That keeps the tool practical rather than overpromising precision.'],
  ['what-is-a-virtual-wardrobe-app','What is a virtual wardrobe app?','what is a virtual wardrobe app','A virtual wardrobe app is a digital version of your closet. It stores clothing images and helps you see, combine and plan the pieces you own.','Why it helps','Most people forget useful pieces once they are out of sight. A visual wardrobe makes it easier to spot repeats, plan for a specific event and make more use of purchases you already made.','What to look for',['Easy ways to add clothes.','Outfit building for real occasions.','A clear view of your own pieces, not only shopping suggestions.','Tools that make the closet faster to use over time.'],'Style BFF goes beyond inventory','Style BFF adds an AI personal stylist layer: it uses your profile and digital wardrobe to suggest occasion outfits, plus virtual try-on for supported inspiration and store links.'],
  ['how-to-stop-buying-clothes-you-never-wear','How to stop buying clothes you never wear','how to stop buying clothes you never wear','Buy fewer clothes you will not wear by making each purchase answer a real wardrobe need. Before checkout, check whether the item suits you, fits your life and creates several outfits with what you own.','Use the three-outfit rule','Before buying, name three outfits you can create with the item using your existing wardrobe. If you cannot, it may be an attractive isolated piece rather than a useful addition.','Check your real habits','Buy for the life you live now—not an imagined future event. Consider comfort, care needs, footwear and whether you own the layer the garment needs.','Use Style BFF before you buy','Try a supported product or inspiration link on yourself in Style BFF. Then check how the direction works with your Style Profile and your digital wardrobe.'],
  ['how-to-rebuild-your-style-after-a-life-change','How to rebuild your style after a life change','how to rebuild your style','Rebuilding your style after a new job, move, body change or new routine starts with clarity, not a complete wardrobe replacement. Keep what still feels like you and rebuild around the life you live now.','Take stock without judgment','Separate clothes into keep, unsure and no-longer-you groups. Notice what you wear when you need confidence and what no longer suits your day-to-day routine.','Choose a new direction','Use a few words for the feeling you want—perhaps polished, relaxed, creative or minimal. Then collect references that reflect that direction without copying someone else’s entire wardrobe.','Use Style BFF as a practical starting point','Your Style Profile, occasion outfits and virtual try-on can help you test a new direction on yourself before you commit to a closet overhaul.'],
  ['what-to-pack-for-a-trip-from-your-own-closet','What to pack for a trip from your own closet','what to pack for a trip','Pack by outfit combinations, not individual items. Start with the activities and weather, choose a small color story, then make sure each layer and shoe works across more than one look.','Plan for the actual itinerary','List travel days, dinners, work moments, outdoor time and one backup scenario. This gives every item a job and prevents packing for vague possibilities.','Build around repeatable pieces',['Choose two or three bottoms that work with several tops.','Bring one outer layer that matches every look.','Limit shoes to pairs that work across the full plan.'],'Use your digital wardrobe first','Style BFF can help build combinations from the clothes you own, making it easier to see a small set of outfits before you start putting items in a suitcase.'],
  ['how-to-create-a-capsule-wardrobe-that-feels-like-you','How to create a capsule wardrobe that feels like you','how to create a capsule wardrobe','A useful capsule wardrobe is not a rigid number of beige basics. It is a small group of clothes that suit you, work together and match your real schedule.','Start with your life','Count the settings you dress for most: work, casual days, social plans, travel or parenting. Your capsule should reflect those proportions rather than someone else’s shopping list.','Build a personal color story','Choose colors you enjoy wearing near your face, then add neutrals and accents that combine easily. Style BFF’s Style Profile can offer a practical starting point for this.','Keep it flexible','A capsule should make dressing easier, not remove your personality. Add favorite textures, prints and statement pieces when they still connect to several outfits.'],
  ['best-virtual-try-on-apps','Best virtual try-on apps: what to look for','best virtual try-on app','The best virtual try-on app is the one that answers your actual question. Some tools preview a garment on a model or avatar; Style BFF is designed for people who want to explore a look on their own photo alongside personal styling.','Compare the kind of preview','Ask whether the app uses a stock model, an avatar or your uploaded photo. Also check whether it supports a single product, a full outfit, your own closet or a saved link from elsewhere.','Check the surrounding workflow','A preview is more valuable when you can save it, compare alternatives and connect it to your wardrobe, occasion and personal preferences.','Where Style BFF fits','Style BFF combines supported-link try-on with a Style Profile, occasion outfit ideas and a digital wardrobe. It is a strong choice when you want the preview to lead to a real getting-dressed decision.'],
  ['style-bff-vs-whering-which-closet-app','Style BFF vs Whering: which closet app?','Style BFF vs Whering','Style BFF and Whering solve different parts of the wardrobe problem. Style BFF focuses on personal styling, occasion outfits and visual try-on on your own photo; Whering is known for digital wardrobe organization and wardrobe tracking.','Choose based on your daily question','Choose a closet-tracking tool if your main goal is logging wears and organizing inventory. Choose a styling-first tool if you want help deciding what suits you and what to wear next.','What Style BFF is built to do','Style BFF combines a Style Profile, a digital wardrobe, occasion-based ideas and try-on from supported inspiration or store links. It is designed to turn your wardrobe into decisions, not only data.','Verify current features before paying','App features and pricing change. Check current store listings and choose the app whose workflow matches the job you will use every week.'],
  ['style-bff-vs-acloset-which-ai-closet-app','Style BFF vs Acloset: which AI closet app?','Style BFF vs Acloset','Style BFF is built around personal style guidance, outfits for occasions and seeing saved looks on your own photo. Acloset is commonly used for digital wardrobe organization and outfit planning.','Compare your starting point','If you want to organize a large wardrobe quickly, check the closet setup tools first. If your main problem is deciding what suits you or whether a saved look works on you, choose a styling workflow that starts with those questions.','Where Style BFF is strongest','Style BFF brings together a Style Profile, a wardrobe, occasion-based suggestions and supported-link virtual try-on. The focus is a personal visual answer, not only a catalog of clothes.','Use current listings for final decisions','Availability, pricing and exact capabilities can change. Verify both apps in their current app-store listings before subscribing.'],
  ['style-bff-vs-style-dna','Style BFF vs Style DNA: which styling app?','Style BFF vs Style DNA','Style BFF is designed for people who want personal guidance plus a digital wardrobe, occasion outfits and visual try-on from supported links. Style DNA is widely associated with color and style analysis.','Start with your main problem','Choose a color-analysis-focused workflow when your goal is primarily understanding your palette. Choose a broader styling workflow when you want to turn that guidance into outfits, wardrobe decisions and visual try-on.','Why Style BFF is a complete loop','Style BFF helps users understand what suits them, build a wardrobe view, choose looks for an occasion and try saved inspiration on themselves.','Keep comparisons fair','Both products evolve. Confirm current store descriptions, pricing and features before making a purchase decision.'],
  ['best-digital-wardrobe-app','Best digital wardrobe app: how to choose','best digital wardrobe app','The best digital wardrobe app depends on whether you primarily want to catalog clothes, track wears, get outfit ideas or see new looks on yourself. Style BFF is designed for the person who wants wardrobe organization connected to personal styling and virtual try-on.','Compare the job each app does','Whering emphasizes wardrobe visibility, community and wear tracking. Acloset emphasizes AI-led closet digitization and daily planning. Indyx pairs a digital wardrobe with human styling. Pureple emphasizes outfit planning and filters.','Choose a wardrobe that leads to action','A closet database is only useful if it helps you decide what to wear, what to pack and what not to buy. Look for the input method, occasions, planning tools and how easily you can return to saved outfits.','Where Style BFF fits','Style BFF brings a Style Profile, digital wardrobe, occasion outfits and supported-link try-on into one workflow. It is best suited to people who want the wardrobe to answer “what suits me and what should I wear next?”'],
  ['style-bff-vs-alta','Style BFF vs Alta: which AI stylist?','Style BFF vs Alta','Alta and Style BFF both list AI styling and digital wardrobe tools. Alta’s listing emphasizes daily planning, a virtual avatar and trip planning; Style BFF centers a Style Profile, occasion looks from your wardrobe and supported-link try-on on your own photo.','What Alta is built around','Alta’s official product page lists a digital closet, daily recommendations, weather, trip packing, a style calendar, a wishlist and avatar try-on.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF starts with what suits you, then applies it to your wardrobe, real occasion and saved inspiration. Its supported-link try-on lets you check a Pinterest, Instagram or store look on your own photo.','The practical difference','Alta is oriented around avatar and planning tools. Style BFF is designed for personal profile guidance, wardrobe-based occasion looks and direct inspiration-to-your-photo try-on.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://www.altadaily.com/" rel="nofollow">Alta official product page</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-indyx','Style BFF vs Indyx: AI or human stylist?','Style BFF vs Indyx','Style BFF and Indyx use a digital wardrobe differently. Style BFF is an AI personal stylist with a Style Profile, occasion looks and virtual try-on; Indyx lists a digital wardrobe and paid one-to-one human styling.','What Indyx is built around','Indyx lists digital-wardrobe tools, outfit planning, packing lists, wear tracking, social features and paid access to personal stylists.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF provides an always-available AI workflow: learn what suits you, scan selected gallery photos to organize your wardrobe, get occasion looks and try supported saved inspiration on your own photo.','The practical difference','Indyx includes paid human-stylist services. Style BFF is built for immediate AI-led personal guidance, wardrobe-based occasion looks and visual try-on without scheduling a session.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://www.myindyx.com/" rel="nofollow">Indyx official product page</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-pureple','Style BFF vs Pureple: which wardrobe app?','Style BFF vs Pureple','Pureple and Style BFF both help organize clothes. Pureple focuses on closet organization, filters and weather-aware suggestions; Style BFF adds a Style Profile, wardrobe-based occasion looks and supported-link try-on on your own photo.','What Pureple is built around','Pureple’s official page lists a virtual closet, item recognition, outfit suggestions, weather-aware recommendations and organization by season, occasion and color.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF is made for the personal styling question: what suits you, what should you wear for this plan and how would a saved look work on you? Its digital wardrobe is used to create looks, not simply store inventory.','The practical difference','Pureple emphasizes closet filters and planning. Style BFF combines personal styling inputs, occasion looks from what you own and visual try-on in the same workflow.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://pureple.com/" rel="nofollow">Pureple official product page</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-combyne','Style BFF vs Combyne: which fashion app?','Style BFF vs Combyne','Combyne and Style BFF serve different fashion tasks. Combyne lists outfit collages, inspiration, saved wardrobe and shopping; Style BFF is an AI personal stylist for understanding what suits you and previewing supported looks on yourself.','What Combyne is built around','Combyne’s official site lists outfit creation from fashion pieces, community inspiration, saved wardrobe and direct shopping from brands.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF turns inspiration into a personal decision: organize your digital wardrobe, choose an occasion, then use a supported Pinterest, Instagram or store link to see how a look direction works on your own photo.','The practical difference','Combyne is centered on fashion discovery and collage creation. Style BFF is built to answer what suits you and what to wear from your own wardrobe.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://www.combyne.com/" rel="nofollow">Combyne official product page</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-acloset-in-depth','Style BFF vs Acloset: in-depth comparison','Style BFF vs Acloset','Acloset and Style BFF both list AI wardrobe and outfit tools. Acloset emphasizes wardrobe digitization, purchase imports, planning and analytics; Style BFF is built around personal style guidance, occasion looks from your own wardrobe and supported-link try-on on your own photo.','What Acloset is built around','Acloset’s official materials list clothing detection, purchase imports, a digital closet, weather and occasion recommendations, try-on, style chat, travel planning and style statistics.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF focuses on the personal styling loop: learn what suits you, scan selected gallery photos to organize your wardrobe, choose a look for an occasion and try a saved Pinterest, Instagram or store direction on your own photo.','The practical difference','Acloset emphasizes imports, item management and analytics. Style BFF makes personal style direction, wardrobe-based occasion looks and visual try-on the central workflow.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://www.acloset.app/" rel="nofollow">Acloset official product page</a> and <a class="source" href="https://www.acloset.app/support/" rel="nofollow">Acloset support documentation</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-whering-in-depth','Style BFF vs Whering: in-depth comparison','Style BFF vs Whering','Whering and Style BFF both help you use clothes you own. Whering is centered on cataloging, wear tracking, packing and community; Style BFF is an AI personal stylist centered on what suits you, occasion looks and visual try-on on your own photo.','What Whering is built around','Whering’s official site lists wardrobe adding, digital organization, outfit planning, wardrobe insights, packing and community features such as styling friends and shared wardrobes.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF turns saved inspiration into a personal answer. Its Style Profile and supported-link try-on let you see whether a Pinterest, Instagram or store look works on you, not only as a flat outfit.','The practical difference','Whering emphasizes tracking and community features. Style BFF centers personal profile guidance, wardrobe-based occasion looks and previewing supported looks on your own photo.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://www.whering.co/" rel="nofollow">Whering official product page</a>.</p>'],
  ['best-virtual-try-on-apps-in-depth','Best virtual try-on apps: an honest guide','best virtual try-on apps','The best virtual try-on app depends on the preview you need. Some apps use an avatar, some dress a model and some generate a look from your own photo. Style BFF is designed for people who want to take inspiration from supported links and see the direction on themselves in a broader styling workflow.','Ask what is actually being tried on','Before choosing an app, check whether you can preview one garment, a full outfit, pieces from your closet or a look from a link. Also ask whether the image uses a stock model, an avatar or your uploaded photo.','Compare the workflow around the image','A try-on is more useful when it connects to your colors, body guidance, occasion and wardrobe. It should help you decide whether to wear, save or buy the look—not only generate a picture.','Why Style BFF belongs in the shortlist','Style BFF combines a personal Style Profile, digital wardrobe, occasion outfit ideas and supported Pinterest, Instagram and store-link try-on on your own photo. Use it when you want a styling decision rather than a standalone generated image.'],
  ['style-bff-vs-aesty','Style BFF vs Aesty: which AI stylist?','Style BFF vs Aesty','Aesty and Style BFF both list personal styling, a digital closet and social-inspiration try-on. Aesty is listed for iPhone and describes an avatar, screenshot-based styling, moodboards and closet planning; Style BFF is available on iOS and Android and centers a Style Profile, occasion looks from your wardrobe and supported-link try-on on your own photo.','What Aesty is built around','Aesty’s App Store listing says it turns Instagram, TikTok and Pinterest screenshots into looks, previews them on an avatar, combines them with a digital closet, and includes closet sharing and AI-stylist tools.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF gives iOS and Android users a direct personal styling loop: learn what suits you, scan selected gallery photos to organize your wardrobe, get looks for an occasion and preview a supported Pinterest, Instagram or store look on your own photo.','The practical difference','Aesty uses an iPhone-first avatar and moodboard flow. Style BFF is cross-platform and is designed to move from your Style Profile and wardrobe to an occasion look and a direct inspiration-link-to-your-photo preview.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/aesty-ai-stylist-planner/id6502579395" rel="nofollow">Aesty on the App Store</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-drape','Style BFF vs Drape: which closet app?','Style BFF vs Drape','Drape and Style BFF both address daily outfit planning with a digital wardrobe and AI styling. Drape is listed for iPhone and focuses on closet scanning, weather, outfit planning and AI try-on; Style BFF adds a Style Profile, supported social and store links, and iOS and Android availability.','What Drape is built around','Drape’s App Store page lists AI closet organization, daily outfit recommendations from clothes you own, weather-aware planning, an outfit builder and a try-on preview on your body.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF connects your colors, body guidance, preferences, occasions, digital wardrobe and saved online inspiration, so you can see whether a look found elsewhere suits you before you wear or buy it.','The practical difference','Drape is limited to iPhone in its current listing. Style BFF works across iOS and Android and combines personal style analysis, wardrobe-based occasion looks and supported-link try-on.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://apps.apple.com/us/app/drape-outfit-planner-closet/id6761688732" rel="nofollow">Drape on the App Store</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-kynto','Style BFF vs Kynto: which try-on app?','Style BFF vs Kynto','Kynto and Style BFF both combine virtual try-on with a digital closet. Kynto is an Android app that lists clothing scans, website imports, outfit collections and occasion ideas; Style BFF adds a Style Profile and supported Pinterest, Instagram and store-link try-on on the user’s own photo.','What Kynto is built around','Kynto’s Google Play listing lists a digital closet, scanned or website-imported clothing, side-by-side try-on, occasion outfit collections and AI styling suggestions.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF starts with the person: understand what suits you, scan selected gallery photos to organize your wardrobe, get an occasion look, and turn supported saved inspiration into a try-on on your own photo.','The practical difference','Kynto emphasizes importing and comparing items. Style BFF is cross-platform and centers color and body guidance, wardrobe-based occasion looks and link-based try-on.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.zoozoo.kynto" rel="nofollow">Kynto on Google Play</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-clorg','Style BFF vs Clorg: which closet app?','Style BFF vs Clorg','Clorg and Style BFF both list a digital wardrobe with virtual try-on on your own photo. Clorg is an Android closet organizer focused on building outfits from cataloged clothes; Style BFF adds Style Profile guidance, wardrobe-based occasion looks and supported Pinterest, Instagram and store-link try-on across iOS and Android.','What Clorg is built around','Clorg’s Google Play listing lists background removal and tagging, a searchable digital wardrobe and full-outfit virtual try-on using the user’s body photo.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF connects the preview to personal styling: color and body guidance, the occasion you are dressing for, your digital wardrobe and saved online inspiration.','The practical difference','Clorg focuses on Android closet organization and outfit construction. Style BFF is cross-platform and begins with what suits you, then makes wardrobe-based occasion looks and supported-link try-on available in one workflow.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.clorg.app" rel="nofollow">Clorg on Google Play</a>.</p>'],
  ['style-bff-vs-wearmatch','Style BFF vs WearMatch: which AI stylist?','Style BFF vs WearMatch','WearMatch and Style BFF both list AI styling, digital closet tools, color guidance and virtual try-on on a user photo. WearMatch’s Google Play page emphasizes styling feedback, a collection feed and photo or persona try-on; Style BFF centers a direct Style Profile, wardrobe-based occasion looks and supported links from Pinterest, Instagram and stores.','What WearMatch is built around','WearMatch’s Google Play listing lists a seasonal palette, digital closet, own-photo or AI-persona try-on, outfit checks and a styling feed.','Why Style BFF is the better everyday styling workflow','Style BFF is designed to answer the next question: what suits you, what should you wear for an occasion, what can you make from your closet and how does a saved online look work on you?','The practical difference','WearMatch emphasizes feed discovery and outfit scoring. Style BFF is cross-platform and centers a Style Profile, wardrobe-based occasion styling and direct try-on from supported saved links.','<p>Current product details: <a class="source" href="https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.wearmatch" rel="nofollow">WearMatch on Google Play</a>.</p>'],
  ['best-ai-stylist-apps-ios-android','Best AI stylist apps for iPhone and Android','best AI stylist apps for iPhone and Android','The best AI stylist app for iPhone or Android depends on whether you need a digital wardrobe, outfit planning, human styling, virtual try-on or personal style guidance. Style BFF is built to combine those everyday decisions across both iOS and Android.','Check platform before features','Some comparison apps are limited to one marketplace: Aesty and Drape are listed for iPhone, while Kynto, Clorg and WearMatch are listed on Google Play. Style BFF is available across iOS and Android, which matters if you switch devices or share styling with someone on another platform.','Use the feature stack that matches your need','Acloset, Whering, Indyx, Alta and Pureple list different combinations of closet, tracking, human-styling, planning and avatar features. Style BFF combines a Style Profile, wardrobe-based occasion looks and supported-link try-on on your own photo in one workflow.','Why Style BFF leads across platforms','Style BFF is available for iOS and Android, combining a free Style Profile, a digital wardrobe organized from selected gallery photos, occasion outfits from what you own and virtual try-on from supported Pinterest, Instagram and store links on your own photo.']
];

